WEBVTT

1
00:00:09.467 --> 00:00:19.183
By the time Nina got to Kids Central, everyone was already hula hooping.

2
00:00:19.184 --> 00:00:26.583
"Are we having another hula hoop day?" Nina asked excitedly. "Where's Izzie?"

3
00:00:26.584 --> 00:00:29.011
"Izzie wasn't feeling well.

4
00:00:29.012 --> 00:00:33.630
So she stayed home from school today," Miss Shelly told Nina.

5
00:00:33.631 --> 00:00:38.583
"And we are using hula hoops again, but in a different way."

6
00:00:38.584 --> 00:00:44.053
Nina took off her backpack and sat down between Bobby and Ethan.

7
00:00:44.054 --> 00:00:48.681
She smiled at Jason, who was sitting across from her.

8
00:00:48.682 --> 00:00:51.208
"It's almost holiday season.

9
00:00:51.209 --> 00:00:55.530
Did any of you decorate your houses yet?" Miss Shelly asked.

10
00:00:55.531 --> 00:01:00.291
"We put Christmas lights in our front yard," Nina said.

11
00:01:00.292 --> 00:01:04.189
"We put candles in our menorah," Jason said.

12
00:01:04.190 --> 00:01:08.313
"We put up a Christmas tree with lights!" Ethan said.

13
00:01:08.314 --> 00:01:12.956
"Aren't lights and candles a pretty way to spread holiday spirit?

14
00:01:12.957 --> 00:01:20.046
My favorite decoration is a wreath of lights," Miss Shelly said.

15
00:01:20.047 --> 00:01:23.697
She showed them a photo of a bright, white wreath.

16
00:01:23.698 --> 00:01:26.113
It was made of lights!

17
00:01:26.114 --> 00:01:32.085
"Oh! I wish we had a wreath like that in here," Nina whispered.

18
00:01:32.086 --> 00:01:39.224
"We will have a wreath like that after today," Miss Shelly said.

19
00:01:39.225 --> 00:01:47.713
Miss Shelly rolled out the biggest hula hoop Nina had ever seen.

20
00:01:47.714 --> 00:01:53.518
"Whoa! Too bad Izzie isn't here to see this!" Nina said.

21
00:01:53.519 --> 00:01:57.880
"Is that going to be our wreath?" Bobby asked.

22
00:01:57.881 --> 00:02:04.912
"Yes! We'll wrap lights around it," Miss Shelly said.

23
00:02:04.913 --> 00:02:09.268
Miss Shelly opened a box and pulled out a string of lights.

24
00:02:09.269 --> 00:02:12.711
"Tape one end to the hula hoop.

25
00:02:12.712 --> 00:02:18.156
Wrap the rest of the string around the hoop.

26
00:02:18.157 --> 00:02:22.750
When you're done, connect it to another string and keep going!"

27
00:02:22.751 --> 00:02:26.534
Everyone worked hard wrapping lights around the hoop.

28
00:02:26.535 --> 00:02:33.355
Finally the boxes of lights were empty.

29
00:02:33.356 --> 00:02:37.983
"I can't even see the hula hoop anymore!" Nina said.

30
00:02:37.984 --> 00:02:44.408
"Let's plug in our wreath," Miss Shelly said.

31
00:02:44.409 --> 00:02:48.974
"Wow!" The kids all cried together.

32
00:02:48.975 --> 00:02:55.809
"I bet you can see it from outer space!" Bobby said.

33
00:02:55.810 --> 00:02:58.385
"Why are the lights out in here?"

34
00:02:58.386 --> 00:03:03.252
Ms. Folani stuck her head in the door.

35
00:03:03.253 --> 00:03:05.860
"Is everything okay?"

36
00:03:05.861 --> 00:03:08.460
Then Ms. Folani noticed the wreath.

37
00:03:08.461 --> 00:03:13.917
"That's beautiful! Is this the work of Kids Central?" she asked.

38
00:03:13.918 --> 00:03:17.965
"Yep." Nina nodded proudly.

39
00:03:17.966 --> 00:03:20.570
Miss Shelly looked proud too.

40
00:03:20.571 --> 00:03:25.637
"I know a great spot for that wreath!" Ms. Folani said.

41
00:03:25.638 --> 00:03:28.184
"On the front of our school!

42
00:03:28.185 --> 00:03:30.058
What do you think?"

43
00:03:30.059 --> 00:03:34.344
The principal looked at Nina, Bobby, Ethan, and Jason.

44
00:03:34.345 --> 00:03:39.035
Ethan grinned. "I think it's a great idea!"

45
00:03:39.036 --> 00:03:42.319
"So do I," Jason agreed.

46
00:03:42.320 --> 00:03:46.984
"Hey, aren't you missing somebody?" Ms. Folani asked.

47
00:03:46.985 --> 00:03:50.755
"Izzie stayed home sick today," Nina said.

48
00:03:50.756 --> 00:03:56.488
"But I bet she would say it's a good idea too."

49
00:03:56.489 --> 00:04:01.430
The kids carried the wreath out the front door.

50
00:04:01.431 --> 00:04:03.616
Miss Shelly plugged it in.

51
00:04:03.617 --> 00:04:08.075
The warm glow of the lights reflected off the snowy ground.

52
00:04:08.076 --> 00:04:15.630
Nina couldn't wait to show the wreath to Izzie tomorrow.
